YAAP
==============

Getting Started
---------------

To get started with Android, you'll need to get
familiar with [Git and Repo](http://source.android.com/source/using-repo.html).

To initialize your local repository using the YAAP trees, use a command like this:

```bash
<<<<<<< HEAD
repo init -u https://github.com/yaap/manifest.git -b seventeen --git-lfs
=======
repo init -u https://github.com/sm8735-dev/yaap_manifest.git -b seventeen --git-lfs
>>>>>>> 240d09b (manifest: Track sun repos)
```
Then to sync up:
```bash
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags --optimized-fetch
```

Building the source
---------------

The source at YAAP is well configured for building.

```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
lunch yaap_device-user && m yaap
```
